174
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,320
你给麦肯齐太多主动权了
You've given Mackenzie way too much power,

175
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:36,200
你自己得拽起来
and you need to take some of that power back.

176
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,820
是她的
It's her.

177
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:38,940
把电话给我
Give me the phone.

178
00:06:39,126 --> 00:06:40,960
你就这么说
Here's what you're gonna say --

179
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,660
麦肯齐 我很忙 等会儿你再打来
"Hey, Mackenzie. I'm busy. Call me back later."

180
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,760
-然后你就挂断 -绝对不行
- Then you hang up.- No way!

181
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,020
那你就再也拿不回这手机了
Then you're not getting the phone back.

182
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,220
把它给我
Just give it to me.

183
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,460
麦肯齐 我很忙
"Hey, Mackenzie. I'm busy.

184
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:50,940
等会儿你再打来 然后你就挂断
Call me back later." Then you hang up.

185
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:51,960
-我做不到 -就这么做
- I can't. - Do it.

186
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:52,660
-不行 - 就这么做
- No! - Do it!

187
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:54,480
好吧 去你的
Okay! Damn you.

188
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:59,000
麦肯齐 我很忙 等会儿你再打来
Hey, Mackenzie. I'm busy. Call me back later.

189
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,800
太难了
That was hard.

190
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,120
要是容易的话 谁都能受人欢迎了
If it was easy, everyone would be popular.

191
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:12,720
有人敲门啦
Knock knock!

192
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,880
进来吧 门没关
Come on in! It's open!

193
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:19,320
我带了些旧的童装来给莉莉
I just wanted to drop off these old baby clothes for Lily.

194
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,200
好的 你人太好了
Oh, that's right. You're so sweet.

195
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:22,720
我希望自己来的别不是时候
I hope I didn't come at a bad time.

196
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,440
一点也不
Not at all.

197
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:26,100
我正考虑要带莉莉去哪儿骑车呢
I was just deciding where to take Lily for our bike ride --

198
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,360
湖边还是公园
The lake or the park.

199
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,380
我比较倾向于去公园
I'm leaning towards the park.

200
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,040
我看得出来
I can see that.

201
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,240
你太客气了
You didn't have to do that.

202
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:37,340
你们还真是传统
You guys are a touch old class.

203
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,880
-今晚对你很重要 -法国红酒
- Well, it is a big night for you, so. - French.

204
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,240
这些家伙啊
Those guys.

205
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,820
那你想好要说什么了吗
So, have you given any thought to what you might say?

206
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,340
事实上 我现在正努力不让自己想这事
Oh, actually, I'm trying not to think about my act right now.

207
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,900
说实话 我内心有点挣扎
I'm kind of fighting the old butterflies, to be honest.

208
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:50,940
很正常
That's normal.

209
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:54,240
我听说乔纳斯兄弟在每次演出前都会害怕
I hear The Jonas Brothers get scared before every concert.

210
00:07:54,547 --> 00:07:57,820
凯文不会的吧 那家伙可摇滚了
Not Kevin? The guy's a rock.

211
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,940
尤其是凯文
Especially Kevin.

212
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,120
我真不敢相信我居然给艾丽克斯买过这个
I can't believe I ever bought this for Alex.

213
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:03,620
我真希望当时有人能说点什么
I wish somebody had said something.

214
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,980
别这样啦 这衣服十年前可能很可爱呢
Oh, come on. That was probably cute 10 years ago.

215
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,400
不 不 从来没有
No, no. It never was.

216
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:08,820
你知道的
And you know --

217
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:10,840
我的衣服也是这样
I'm the exact same way about my clothes.

218
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,320
大多数时候 很不错
Most of the time, great.

219
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,760
不过时不时的就会有那么一件例外
But every now and again, there's that one outfit.

220
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:18,380
我真希望当时有人能对我实话实说
I just wish somebody would be honest with me and say,

221
00:08:18,771 --> 00:08:22,119
你的穿着实在是雷人哇
"What you're wearing is inappropriate."

222
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,240
你懂我意思吗
Do you know what I mean?

223
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:25,440
我懂 克莱尔
I think I do, Claire.

224
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
我懂
I think I do.

225
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,160
我的回答是没问题
And my answer is yes.

226
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:29,880
好的
Okay.

227
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,920
我愿意给你打扮
I would love to dress you.

228
00:08:31,957 --> 00:08:34,069
不 我不想要你来帮我打扮
No, it -- I don't want you to dress me.

229
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:34,840
不用
No.

230
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,460
我觉得我该对你坦白
And...I owe it to you to be honest,

231
00:08:37,637 --> 00:08:38,600
所以我要说
so I'm just gonna say

232
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,000
你得丢掉这条单车短裤
that you need to lose the bicycle shorts.

233
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:43,840
你说什么
Excuse me?

234
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,540
小卡 它不适合你
They're not working for you, Cam.

235
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,500
我不是在针对你
Please don't take this personally.

236
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,900
我是说 没人穿单车短裤好看的
I mean, nobody looks good in bike shorts.

237
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:53,160
我只是 我觉得我应该对你坦白
I just -- I feel that I owe it to you to be honest.

238
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,200
这么说 我们还是好朋友 对吧
So, we're good, right?

239
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,526
-我们非常要好 -我们非常要好
- We're great. - We're great.

240
00:08:56,555 --> 00:08:57,619
-我们非常要好 -太好了
- We're great. - Oh, great.

241
00:08:57,658 --> 00:08:58,945
好吧
Okay.

242
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,340
或许你应该穿自己的衣 让别人去说吧
You should probably just show yourself out.

243
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,600
我听见 我听见走廊上有哭声
I hear -- I hear some crying down the hallway.

244
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:06,300
瞧 真是个好父亲
Look at that. That's a good dad.

245
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:07,160
因为有了孩子
Because you've got a baby,

246
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,480
所以一丁点儿小的声音你都能听到
and you hear every little sound.

247
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,391
要是我的话 我根本就不会注意到
I wouldn't have -- I wouldn't have even noticed...

248
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:12,280
有哭声
crying.

249
00:09:16,146 --> 00:09:18,040
好了
Uh, okay. All right.

250
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,440
你们需要知道的是
All you need to know about this one

251
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,900
斯基普·乌森是个著名的房产经纪人
is that Skip Woosnum is a well-known realtor

252
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,180
而且很老了
and he's old.

253
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:23,820
收到
Got it.

254
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,400
斯基普·乌森 房产经纪人 老的
Skip Woosnum. Realtor. Old.

255
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,020
开始了
Here we go.

256
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:30,250
我不是要说斯基普·乌森已经老了
I'm not saying realtor Skip Woosnum is old,

257
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:32,680
不过他卖出去的第一件物业
but the first property he ever sold...

258
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,520
居然是个洞穴
was a cave.

259
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:37,991
你没有
You're not, uh...

260
00:09:38,023 --> 00:09:39,127
没有笑
not laughing.

261
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,740
你怎么不笑 米奇尔叔叔
Why aren't you laughing, uncle Mitchell?

262
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:42,709
因为他觉得不好笑
'cause he doesn't think it's funny,

263
00:09:42,709 --> 00:09:44,480
或者可能你觉得我并不搞笑
or maybe -- maybe you don't think I'm funny.

264
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,240
你是要说这些吗 米奇
Is that what you're saying, Mitch?

265
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:45,820
不是
No, it's...

266
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:51,320
我懂了 我懂了
I just got it!

267
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:53,620
洞穴
Oh. Cave!

268
00:09:53,653 --> 00:09:55,197
-这个是需要点脑力 -没错没错
- That one's kind of a thinker. - Yes!

269
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:04,380
他也来了
There he is.

270
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:06,220
好了
All right, now.

271
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:07,220
少来了 杰
Knock it off, Jay.

272
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,660
这儿你一个人的名字都叫不出来
You don't know anyone's name here.

273
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:09,800
你开什么玩笑
Are you kidding me?

274
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:10,540
卡洛斯
Carlos!

275
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,100
运气不错
Lucky guess.

276
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,980
还好只有一个人回头
I'm lucky only one turned around.

277
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,080
听着 我需要帮助
Listen -- I need a favor.

278
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:23,280
我高估了这个派对上我认识的人数
I overestimated the number of people I know at this party.

279
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:26,440
你去到处转转 做做自我介绍
So you go around, introduce yourself,

280
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:27,840
我就在旁边偷听他们叫什么
and I'll hear the names.

281
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,360
你知道你是在叫我
You realize you're asking me

282
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,700
帮你证明我亲妈是错的
to help prove my own mother wrong.

283
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:33,040
你每介绍一次 我就给你两美金
I'll pay two bucks per introduction.

284
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:34,220
好吧 那是拉蒙纳
All right, well, that's Ramona.

285
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,440
她狂爱饮烈酒
She's crazy for bingo.

286
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:36,180
拉蒙纳
Ramona.

287
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,000
歌洛莉亚
Gloria!

288
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,340
别那么不合群了
Stop being such a snob.

289
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,300
过来见见我的朋友夏利奥和他的太太
Come over and meet my friend Julio and his wife --

290
00:10:58,347 --> 00:11:00,998
对不起 你说你叫什么
uh, I'm sorry. Your name again?

291
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:01,300
凯
Kay?

292
00:11:01,342 --> 00:11:03,623
我觉得你跟凯会很合得来的
I think you're really gonna hit it off with Kay!

293
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:10,720
我是说 她要教我怎么打扮吗
I mean, she's gonna tell me how to dress?!

294
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:12,420
她应该干点她更擅长的
She ought to stick to things she knows more about,

295
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,660
像是怎么把三文鱼烤焦
like overcooking salmon.

296
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:14,260
好吧 等等
Okay, wait.

297
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,160
那么 她真的跟你说
So, she actually said

298
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:17,400
你穿单车裤不好看吗
that you don't look good in bicycle shorts?

299
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,040
是的
Yes.

300
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,060
你穿单车裤不好看
"You don't look good in bicycle shorts".

301
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:23,500
疯了
Madness.

302
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:26,380
是她
Oh, and here she is.

303
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:27,860
好吧 我不能在这待着了
Okay, you know what? I can't be here.

304
00:11:27,892 --> 00:11:29,572
我要 我要出去透透气
I'm -- I'm going out for some air.

305
00:11:29,604 --> 00:11:32,065
好的 去吧 我也许会跟她吵起来
Yes. Yes, go. This -- this could get ugly.

306
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,640
你好 克莱尔
Hello, Claire.

307
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:35,560
你这个没种的家伙
You are a gutless weasel.

308
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,060
是的 不
Oh, yeah. No.

309
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:38,680
我知道你跟我男人说了什么
I heard what you said to my boyfriend.

310
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:41,080
你跟菲尔说他超搞笑的
You told Phil he was hysterical!

311
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,460
你说他是新一代的理查德·普赖尔
You said he was this generation's Richard Pryor!

312
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:46,880
你该道歉的人不是我
Well, I am not the one that you need to apologize to.

313
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,940
你在胡说什么 你欠我一个谋杀
What are you babbling about? You owe me a murder.

314
00:11:51,191 --> 00:11:53,180
好吧 克莱尔 我做不来
Okay, Claire, I c -- I couldn't do it.

315
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:54,300
我没办法打破菲尔的美梦
I couldn't crush Phil's dreams.

316
00:11:54,660 --> 00:11:57,620
我们说好了的 我跟小卡说单车裤的事
We had a deal. I told Cam about the bike shorts.

317
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,300
不 不
No! No!

318
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,920
我们说好的是 你让小卡脱掉那条热裤
The deal was to get Cam to take off the bike shorts.

319
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,160
可结果呢 他还穿着那条愚蠢的单车热裤
But guess what -- he is still in the stupid bike shorts.

320
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,180
我待会打回给你好吗
Can I call you back?

321
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,120
小卡原来一直都在
Turns out Cam was here the whole time,

322
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,460
他听到了我说的话
and he just heard everything I said.

323
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:11,960
他跑到卧室里哭去了吗
Ooh. Did he just run into the bedroom and cry?

324
00:12:12,003 --> 00:12:13,577
是啊 好像所有同性恋男人都这样
Oh, yes, 'cause that's what all gay men do.

325
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:15,280
我们都如此软弱
We all dissolve into --

326
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,800
好吧 他还真就这么做了
Yes. That is what he did.

327
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,900
每段婚姻都有一些挑战
There are challenging moments in every marriage.

328
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:29,000
为了你丈夫不在众人面前出丑
Um...having to tell your husband that he's not funny

329
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,740
而必须告诉他 他其实一点也不搞笑
so that he won't humiliate himself

330
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:32,340
这绝对是最难的挑战之一了
has to be one of the toughest.

331
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,620
于是我就换了种方式
So I went a different way.

332
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:41,700
别再说了
Stop talking.

333
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:44,740
我只是需要时间来让这个伤口结疤
I just need some time for this wound to become a scar.

334
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,520
对不起我把克莱尔也扯了进来
I'm sorry I got Claire involved,

335
00:12:46,555 --> 00:12:48,260
但是 我不是想批评你
But -- and this is not a criticism,

336
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:51,060
但是有时候你对你的外型
but sometimes you can be a little sensitive

337
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,380
太过于敏感了
about your...appearance.

338
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,980
这就是批评
Well, this is a criticism --

339
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,660
有时你对所有事情都太不敏感了
sometimes you can be insensitive about everything.

340
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,840
我只是觉得 我们的感情足够坚固
I just can't -- I just feel like

341
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:01,540
经得起一点坦诚的考验
our relationship's strong enough to survive a little candor.

342
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:03,000
如果我有什么让你不满意的
I mean, look, you could tell me

343
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,540
你就可以直说
if there's something about me you'd like to change.

344
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:05,480
我讨厌你的胡子
I hate your beard.

345
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,940
你还留了这么一手
Well, you had that bullet in the chamber.

346
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,620
我从来没说过 是因为我不想伤害你
I never said anything because I never wanted to hurt you...

347
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,240
但是我一直觉得你的胡子很烦人
but I've always found your beard off-putting.

348
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,140
是吧 小心脏疼死了吧
See? Hurts.

349
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,160
米奇尔
Mitchell?

350
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:29,340
米奇尔 回来
Mitchell, get back here!

351
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:33,960
你在干吗
What are you doing?

352
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,560
我要把胡子剃了
I'm shaving off the beard.

353
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:36,800
你认真的吗
Seriously?

354
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:41,120
当然 我家男人不喜欢 那就剃掉
Yeah, well, the man I love doesn't like it, so off it goes.

355
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:41,620
好
Well, good.

356
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:42,860
-好的 -很好
-Good. - Great.

357
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,200
很好 那好
Great. Okay.

358
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:46,800
一
One...

359
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:47,240
二
two...

360
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,120
三
three.

361
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:51,640
住手
Wait!

362
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,020
对我来说 你肯这么做已经足够了
The fact that you're willing to do it is enough for me.

363
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:56,620
我爱你的胡子
I love your beard.

364
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:59,980
我喜欢你喝卡布奇诺时 会沾上奶油
I love that when you drink cappuccino, you get foam in it

365
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:01,380
还有你紧张的时候
and when you're nervous, your little...

366
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,800
你的小胡子会抖
hairs twitch.

367
00:14:04,315 --> 00:14:06,240
你就不能在我刮掉这块之前说吗
Well, you couldn't have told me before took a notch out?

368
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:08,560
对不起 听着
I'm sorry. I -- I -- listen.

369
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:13,040
我知道 我对于这个 有些太敏感
I know... I can be touchy about... this.

370
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,340
但是你是个超级大帅哥
But you're this amazing-looking guy, and --

371
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:18,040
我不帅
I am not amazing -

372
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,520
是实话吗
Really?

373
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,200
我不想改变你的任何一点
I wouldn't change anything.

374
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,760
你要知道我每天醒来
You should know that every day,

375
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,660
都因为我的生命中有你而心怀感激
I wake up very grateful to have you in my life.

376
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,200
我才是幸运儿 帅哥
I'm the one who got lucky, handsome.

377
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,400
也许是我表达的不够
Maybe I just don't show it enough.

378
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,720
你可以服务一下我的肩膀作为补偿
Well, you can make it up to me by doing my shoulders.

379
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:35,680
当然
Sure.

380
00:14:43,165 --> 00:14:45,744
我是指按摩 你在想什么
I meant a massage. What are you saying?

381
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:47,780
米奇尔 米奇尔
Oh, Mitchell. Mitchell.

382
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:54,540
是麦肯齐
It's Mackenzie.

383
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:55,200
又是她
Again.

384
00:14:55,245 --> 00:14:57,320
她想让我参加她办的派对
She wants me to come to this party she's throwing.

385
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,180
她之前发过短信给我
She texted me earlier.

386
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,980
你回她短信了 对吧
You texted her back, right?

387
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:00,900
才没有
No.

388
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:03,700
我感到
I'm...

389
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,220
孺子可教也
proud?

390
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,840
-跟她说你会尽量抽时间去 -好
- Tell her you'll try and come. - Right.

391
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:08,200
然后等她说
And then when she says --

392
00:15:08,219 --> 00:15:08,681
海莉
Haley...

393
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,220
我知道怎么做
I got this.

394
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,420
你是哪位
Who's this?

395
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:15,520
干的漂亮
Brilliant.

396
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:19,180
不 我没看到 我短信太多了
No, I didn't see it. I get a lot of texts.

397
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,940
果然是姐妹
I have a sister.

398
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,340
派对是什么时候
When's the party?

399
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:27,100
我会尽量抽空去
I'll try and come.

400
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:29,400
你知道我很忙的 我有自己的生活
You know, I'm kind of busy. I have a life.

401
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,620
有很多事做
You know, stuff.

402
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:32,480
还有作业
Homework.

403
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:33,540
完了
Uh-oh.

404
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,360
我是说 作业算什么
I mean, not homework.

405
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,460
对于爱学习的人来说 算什么呀
It's not work if you love it.

406
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,860
天啊 挂掉 挂掉
Oh, god. Hang up. Hang up.

407
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:39,720
闭嘴
Shut up!

408
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,060
没说你 麦肯齐
Not you, Mackenzie.

409
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:42,800
赶紧把电话扔地上踢过来
Drop the phone and kick it over here!

410
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:43,880
我得挂电话了
Um, I have to go.

411
00:15:43,930 --> 00:15:45,482
晚点我再打给你
I-I'll call you later.

412
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,740
或者你打给人家也行
Or you call me later.

413
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:47,540
爱你
Love you!

414
00:15:47,584 --> 00:15:48,794
发花痴
Aah! Aah!

415
00:15:48,827 --> 00:15:50,510
跟着发花痴
Aah! Aah!

416
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:52,460
刚才还在呢
They were right in here!

417
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:54,380
我知道 我们哪都找遍了
I know, and we looked everywhere, honey,

418
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:55,540
要淡定
so just calm down.

419
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:57,380
淡定皆浮云
Are you kidding me? "Calm down"?

420
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,020
一分钟后
In one minute,

421
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,720
我就要上台了 就像一个
I'm gonna be standing up there like...

422
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:00,720
像个
like a...

423
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:03,520
天哪 我词穷了
Oh, my God. I have no material at all.

424
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:05,500
没事 你一定行的 你不需要准备笑话的
Okay. You're gonna be fine. You don't need jokes.

425
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,320
听我说 亲爱的
Listen to me, honey.

426
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,620
走上台去 展现自己迷人的那面
Get up there. Be your charming self.

427
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:11,580
发自肺腑地来个自我介绍
Make the introductions from your heart, and get out.

428
00:16:11,612 --> 00:16:14,134
你会表现得很犀利的 好吗
You're gonna -- You're gonna be amazing, okay?

429
00:16:14,361 --> 00:16:15,800
菲尔·邓菲
Phil Dunphy.

430
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:16,640
上吧 上吧
Go. Go.

431
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:29,720
各位晚上好
Good evening.

432
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,800
我今天之所以
I would not be here tonight

433
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,140
能够站在这里讲话
if not for the hard work

434
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,186
多亏了南加州房产经纪人董事会的大力支持
of the S.C.A.R.B. Board of trustees...

435
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:36,400
我的笑话没了
I didn't have my jokes.

436
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:38,880
除了直抒胸意以外还有别的选择吗
What choice does a guy have but to play it straight?

437
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:41,580
来自家庭的支持
...the support of my family,

438
00:16:41,623 --> 00:16:44,800
以及吉尔·索普的结肠
and Gil Thorpe's colon.

439
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:55,840
不过菲尔·邓菲可不是那种直抒胸意的人
But Phil Dunphy is no straight guy.

440
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:01,220
今晚在坐的有这么多地产经纪业的巨匠
So many giants of residential real estate here tonight.

441
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:03,360
当然 还有小小约翰麦克宾
And, of course, J.J. McCubbin.

442
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,340
我不是说小小麦是个头矮小
I'm not saying J.J. is small,

443
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:13,700
但在房地产业界 他被描述为犀利哥
but in the realty section, he was described as "Charming."

444
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,500
马克·西蒙 你在吗
Mark Simon, you out there?

445
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:20,940
马可在那 你好吗 伙计
There's Mark. How are you, buddy?

446
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,860
马可最近住进了一套新的样板房
Mark recently moved into a new model.

447
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,500
过得如何 家庭妇男
How are you, Francine?

448
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:31,180
我开玩笑的 马克·西蒙
I kid, Mark Simon. I kid, Mark Simon.

449
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,903
你懂的
You know that.

450
00:17:33,378 --> 00:17:37,200
特兰西科 小马努 还有卡洛斯 这是我妻子歌洛莉亚
Trancito, Little Manuel, and Carlos, my wife, Gloria.

451
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:37,800
幸会
Nice to meet you.

452
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,600
我们得谈谈
We have to talk.

453
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,180
失陪下
Un momento.

454
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:40,920
好的
Mm.

455
00:17:41,847 --> 00:17:42,880
我知道吗 我
You know, I --

456
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,660
真不敢相信你完全没印象
I can't believe you never met them.

457
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,660
你从没接触过这里的任何人
You've never met any of these people.

458
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:48,360
这房间所有的人你都不认识
You don't know anyone in this room.

459
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,130
走吧 杰
Vamos, Jay.

460
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:50,960
要走也要在父女共舞后再走
I'm not leaving before the father/daughter dance.

461
00:17:51,140 --> 00:17:53,560
此外 你所谓的这些人
And "These people," As you call them,

462
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:54,400
不仅仅是雇员
are not just employees.

463
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,173
是个大家庭 或者称为家人
They're mi familia, or "My family."

464
00:17:56,173 --> 00:17:57,454
我懂我的母语 杰
I know what "Mi familia" is, Jay.

465
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,820
他说的我可听不懂
Oh, I was afraid of this.

466
00:18:08,086 --> 00:18:09,841
别去 杰
No. Jay. No.

467
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,120
谢谢你
Thank you. Thank you.

468
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,060
女士们先生们 非常感谢你们
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen. Thank you very much.

469
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,340
我简单说几句
I'm gonna make this brief.

470
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,700
我知道你们中的大部分人甚至不知道我是谁
I know a lot of you out there don't even know who I am.

471
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,660
正如我的爱妻歌洛莉亚所指出的那样
As my lovely wife, Gloria, pointed out,

472
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:22,860
错不在你们 在我
That's my fault, not yours.

473
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,020
我是杰·普里契特
I'm Jay Pritchett,

474
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:25,780
你们的老板
El jefe.

475
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,620
听着 在如此欢乐的时刻
Listen -- on this very, very happy occasion,

476
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:32,520
今天我请客
I'd like to pick up the tab on the bar.

477
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:40,500
你们知道吗 在我建立公司之初
You know, when I started this company...

478
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,340
我所 的第一件事
...the first thing that I --

479
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:43,460
怎么
What?

480
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,720
对了 很好 是的 现在
Oh, right. Right, now. Good. Yeah.

481
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,920
今晚我不是主角
This is not about me.

482
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:49,000
主角是一位非常出众的年轻女士
This is about a very special young lady

483
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,620
以及一位世上最爱她的男人
And the man who loves her more than anyone else on earth.

484
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,020
多温馨啊
Isn't that lovely?

485
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,700
那是件多有爱的事情啊
That's a beautiful, beautiful thing.

486
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,940
你们知道吗 这让我想起了
You know, I'm reminded

487
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,740
当初我和我的小宝贝一起跳舞
of when I used to dance with my little girl.

488
00:19:04,773 --> 00:19:06,032
不过不是像这样
But not like that.

489
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:11,440
悠着点 男孩
Slow down, there, muchacho.

490
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,080
别别别别别昏昏昏昏昏昏
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

491
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,680
难道你们在为此喝彩吗 你们在为此鼓掌吗
What, are you applauding this? You're applauding this?

492
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:20,620
我才不管这是哪门子传统
I don't care what kind of tradition this is.

493
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:23,040
给我停下 听到没 停下
This is gonna stop. Hey, hey, hey, hey. No!

494
00:19:23,078 --> 00:19:24,610
什么 难道只有我目睹这一幕吗
No! What? What? Am I the only one seeing this?!

495
00:19:24,639 --> 00:19:25,730
我们
V-v-vamos!

496
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,740
亲爱的 我很认真的告诉过你
I mean, honey, I am not kidding when I tell you

497
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:31,560
坐在我旁边的那个女人都笑岔气了
There was a woman next to me gasping for breath.

498
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:34,220
真的 菲尔 你太搞笑了
Seriously, you were so freaking funny, Phil.

499
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,200
我有看过专业喜剧演员的演出
I have seen professional comedians

500
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,560
也没有如此笑开了锅
Who could never have done that.

501
00:19:37,587 --> 00:19:38,471
你真是一直被模仿 从未被超越啊
You were unbeliev--

502
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:44,200
我知道是你拿走了我的索引卡片 克莱尔
I know it was you, Claire. You stole my index cards.

503
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,860
对不起 真的对不起
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

504
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,300
我以为我是在保护你
I thought I was protecting you.

505
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,440
如果我的计划成功的话
And if my plan had been successful,

506
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:56,540
那我就夺走了你今夜的辉煌了
I would have robbed you of the greatest night ever.

507
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,200
对不起 我真讨厌
I'm sorry I'm awful.

508
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,180
才没呢
You're not awful.

509
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:02,720
是吗
Mm...

510
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:03,760
克莱尔
Claire...

511
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,740
我就爱你处处为我着想这点
I love that you're looking out for me,

512
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:09,400
也知道你为什么要担心我
and know why you worry about me.

513
00:20:09,998 --> 00:20:12,315
但我对今晚早就胸有成竹了
But I knew I had this tonight.

514
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:14,960
我知道了
I know.

515
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,260
只是有的时候我觉得
Sometimes I just think my job

516
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,520
我的工作就是防止邓家人栽跟头
Is to make sure you guys don't fall on your faces.

517
00:20:20,559 --> 00:20:22,756
这对邓菲家族的人来说可不是件容易事儿
That's a hard job in the Dunphy house.

518
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,600
我们丢人是常事
We fall a lot.

519
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:26,520
我知道
I know.

520
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,100
也许你真正的工作是给予安慰 重树我们的信心
Maybe your real job is to be the person who picks us back up.

521
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,160
这方面没人比你更在行了
Nobody does that better than you.

522
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,680
谢谢夸奖
Thank you.

523
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:39,760
艾丽克斯
Alex.

524
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:42,200
我没有朋友
I have no friends.

525
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,280
该你出马了
You're on the clock.

526
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:51,820
好吧
All right.

527
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,060
出什么事情了
What happened?

528
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,200
我的天哪 老妈 笑死我了
Oh, my gosh, mom. You're killing me.

529
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,560
很好笑 对吧
It's pretty good, right?

530
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,860
好笑 你都可以去拉斯维加斯
Pretty good? You could be, like, in Vegas.

531
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:08,639
好吧
Well...

532
00:21:08,639 --> 00:21:10,248
这神马情况
W-w-what's going on there?

533
00:21:10,280 --> 00:21:11,680
老妈刚给我模仿了下
Mom does the funniest impression

534
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,560
那天在超市碰到的怪阿姨
Of that weird lady at the supermarket.

535
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:16,120
我认识她 说来听听
Oh, yeah. I know her. Let's hear it.

536
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,000
好的
Okay. Um...

537
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,120
如果你买两罐泡菜的话
"It's cheaper

538
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:21,320
会更便宜
if you buy two jars of pickles."

539
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,780
简直活灵活现
It's like she's right here!

540
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,850
我懂了
I know! Yeah.

541
00:21:27,890 --> 00:21:29,820
听起来就像原景再现似的
So like she's right here! I know.

542
00:21:29,850 --> 00:21:31,520
其实一点都不像
That's not what she sounds like.
